  ],
  "repo_truth": "Review 6 returned CHANGES_REQUIRED with four Critical and one Required finding: Windows path-based MoveFileExW is not parent-anchored; numeric IDs plus permitted version deltas do not prove live object continuity; zero Windows file IDs and Object ID metadata are not fail-closed; and seven unavoidable HIGH/CRITICAL implementation seams are omitted. The complete pre-remediation 75-path subject is frozen at sha256:fcaf7198f7ac9298925624b7c7b47da4284aa776d62ddd69429386eacbf8705b. The original operator authority requires an implementable non-cooperating-writer protocol and explicitly permits a reviewed journaled/backup design when ordinary path rename is insufficient. Production and selectors remain frozen.",
  "allowed_scope": [
    "Edit only the seven existing HCM-2.3 documentation authority surfaces listed in contracts_and_gates.",
    "Replace Windows MoveFileExW with SetFileInformationByHandle(FileRenameInfo) on a retained DELETE-capable source handle, using a retained destination-parent handle as FILE_RENAME_INFO.RootDirectory, a simple child name, and ReplaceIfExists=FALSE.",
    "Define exact Windows component-walk binding: retain each opened ancestor without FILE_SHARE_DELETE, enumerate the next entry from the retained parent, compare opened child FileId, forbid reparse substitution, and hold source plus destination-parent handles through the mutation and post-observation boundary.",
    "On Unix, retain source file descriptor and both parent dirfds across renameat2; prove the destination object is the same live kernel object as the retained source descriptor before any native-result or authority record.",
    "Reject all-zero Windows FILE_ID_INFORMATION and fail closed when 128-bit IDs are unsupported.",
    "Query FSCTL_GET_OBJECT_ID on the retained Windows handle: only the documented absent result is admissible; Object ID present, unsupported, access denied, or any other error is fail-closed before and after mutation.",
    "Add transaction-local expected-basis.backup for expected-present publication, copied from the retained source handle, preserving bytes and structured metadata fingerprint before the native boundary; keep it evidence-only and never automatically delete or authorize it as canonical.",
    "Require live retained-handle continuity before native-result and committed-marker construction. Recovery without a durable completed continuity record must terminate outputless refused_ambiguous; it may never infer success from reusable numeric identity alone.",
    "Add Windows ancestor/parent/junction races, Unix/Windows same-ID-reuse ABA, zero-ID, Object-ID present/unqueryable/mutation, backup preservation, and crash/recovery vectors plus executable checker assertions.",
    "Record exact GitNexus evidence for all newly omitted HIGH/CRITICAL implementation seams as independent authorization stops."
  ],
  "non_goals": [
    "No crates/** edit, production Rust, selector, handoff record, ledger, archive, preservation worktree, staging, commit, push, or user task hop.",
    "No cleanup of expected-basis.backup or other evidence, no public API, dependency, byte/count limit, stage-order, threat-model, resolver, HCM-2.2, HCM-2.4, Phase 3+, or Phase 4 change.",
    "No check-only repair, MoveFileExW fallback, reusable numeric-ID inference, zero ID, Object ID, unauthenticated adoption/read/restore/delete/cleanup, or native return code as authority.",
    "Do not treat any recorded HIGH/CRITICAL implementation symbol as authorized."
  ],
  "tasks": [
    "Replay the exact 75-path manifest, aggregate, branch, HEAD, active-dispatch self-exclusion, and selected handoff before editing; stop on any mismatch.",
    "Specify the full handle-anchored Windows open/walk/mutation/post-observation protocol, exact access/share/flags, simple-name constraints, FileRenameInfo no-replace behavior, parent-entry enumeration, error classes, diagnostic-only return, and crash classification.",
    "Specify Unix live source-fd continuity and exact destination comparison across every renameat2 claim/publish/restore boundary; numeric identity alone is never authority once the retained source descriptor is lost.",
    "Specify expected-basis.backup exact name, location, creation/no-replace write/fsync, structured metadata and fingerprint journal fields, retention, recovery use, refusal behavior, and cleanup prohibition without adding a success state.",
    "Update structured observations, schema, vectors, and checker for zero FileId refusal, Object ID absent-only policy, live handle continuity, parent/ancestor substitution, same-ID ABA, backup preservation, and recovery without continuity.",
    "Replace every MoveFileExW primitive/vector/flag claim consistently; preserve Unix no-replace, all prior source-race/D=X/metadata rejection coverage, reader withholding, and error precedence.",
    "Record exact UIDs, commands with/without tests, direct callers, affected counts, processes, and modules for rename_store_path, publish_replacement, verify_compare_and_write_path, require_installed_guards_unchanged, observe_installed_output, observe_prepared_replacement, and require_prepared_replacement_unchanged, plus retain all prior stops.",
